\title{semmcci: Monte Carlo Confidence Intervals in Structural Equation Modeling}
\description{
Generates Monte Carlo confidence intervals for free and defined parameters
in models fitted in the structural equation modeling package \code{lavaan}
(Pesigan & Cheung, 2024).
A sampling distribution of the parameter estimates is generated
from the multivariate normal distribution
using the parameter estimates and their sampling covariance matrix.
Confidence limits are the percentiles of the generated distribution
(Preacher & Selig, 2012; MacKinnon et al., 2004).
}
\section{Models fitted in \code{lavaan}}{

\code{\link[=MC]{MC()}} generates Monte Carlo confidence intervals
from a fitted \code{lavaan} model.
\code{\link[=MCMI]{MCMI()}} does the same for a \code{lavaan} model fitted to multiply imputed data.
\code{\link[=MCStd]{MCStd()}} generates Monte Carlo confidence intervals
for the standardized estimates
from the output of \code{\link[=MC]{MC()}} or \code{\link[=MCMI]{MCMI()}}.
}

\section{Other models}{

\code{\link[=MCGeneric]{MCGeneric()}} and \code{\link[=MCFunc]{MCFunc()}} generate Monte Carlo confidence intervals
for functions of parameters
when the estimates and their sampling covariance matrix are supplied.
\code{\link[=Func]{Func()}} does the same for a list of parameters.
}

\section{Methods}{

The \code{coef()}, \code{vcov()}, \code{confint()}, \code{summary()}, and \code{print()} methods are
available for objects of class \code{semmcci}.
}

